## LWJGL's native-library extraction cache, created at runtime when running the client
## (wherever the working directory happened to be when it was run):
.lwjgl/

## Runtime-generated local data (design.md 3.7/3.8) - a game's per-player snapshots/action
## journals, its game-meta file, and a real account store (login/salted password hash) could
## land in any directory a server happens to be launched from, not just server/target. None
## of this has a fixed name/path yet since the actual persistence code doesn't exist yet -
## broaden this once it does (matching the sibling projects' data/accounts.json pattern).
data/

## Client-local settings (design.md 3.8 - volume, resolution, keybindings, etc., never
## server/account state): no fixed filename decided yet - broaden once it exists.
client-settings.json

# Python bytecode from the asset scripts
__pycache__/
# Patch variants: only the picked one per goal is committed (git add -f); the rest stay local
assets-raw/patches/variants/*.png
# Blueprint variants and review sheets: only the picked drawing per component is committed (git add -f)
assets-raw/blueprints/variants/*.png
assets-raw/blueprints/review/
# Front-page art variants and review sheets: only the picked image per job is committed (git add -f)
assets-raw/frontpage/variants/*.png
assets-raw/frontpage/review/
# The splash video's intermediate layers, EffectCraft project and GIF preview (make_splash.py)
assets-raw/splash/build/
# Mission step clips: layers, EffectCraft projects and renders (assets-raw/replay/README.md)
assets-raw/replay/*/build/

# The archive's downloaded originals (some are 30 MB TIFFs): make_archive_assets.py fetches them again.
assets-raw/archive/originals/
